{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## External documentation revalidation checkpoint\n\nThe evidence revision is current `origin/main` commit `98c428ec4237b40897318123b9cb6304e87c70b7`. The following candidates remain pending an independent filter.\n\n- Complete CLI command discovery. The route registry contains 75 visible nonretired routes. The shipped overview lists 52 commands. `scripts/gen_cli_help.py` and its coverage test omit all 21 intercept routes. `rebar help review-plan` and `rebar help config` return unknown while their direct `--help` forms succeed. ADR 0100 and tickets `ammonitoid-senile-nighthawk` and `grapy-cynical-copepod` require every visible canonical command to appear once and both top-level help forms to work.\n- Correct help flag placement in `README.md`. Runtime and ticket `chartreuse-interested-viper` recognize `--help` and `-h` anywhere before `--`. The README states the rejected first-position rule.\n- Correct the client link contract in `README.md` and `docs/user-guide.md`. The maintained model has seven relations including `caused_by`, and `unlink` accepts an optional relation. Tickets `isogonal-wedded-catfish` and `asbestos-lithe-kouprey` record those additions.\n- Correct generic claim examples in `README.md` and `docs/assets/rebar-demo.svg`. Omitted `--assignee` applies `ticket.default_assignee`. An explicit override requires a Jira-resolvable email or account ID. Ticket `weariless-scrapable-mouse` fixed earlier examples but deliberately excluded the README placeholder and did not inspect the demonstration asset.\n- Separate current configuration lookup from design history. `docs/config-reference.md` is generated from the typed schema. `docs/config.md` remains an ADR-style narrative created by epic `nutty-umbra-agony`. The README still sends exhaustive key lookup to the narrative.\n- Remove the old-to-current mutation confirmation comparison from the generated client CLI reference while retaining current output contracts and no-op classification. Ticket `satiated-unrideable-tapeworm` intentionally required that comparison. The ticket and commit now preserve the migration history.\n- Repair truncated MCP summaries at their registrar descriptions and generator. `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` takes one physical source line, which leaves many generated fragments. Ticket `lupine-clearcut-mare` intentionally chose first-line extraction. The revised source would use a concise client paragraph and normalized whitespace.\n- Replace obsolete manual close-gate instructions in `README.md`. The current completion gate verifies before close and signs a passing result after the status write. It supports `--ref` and `--force=<reason>`. Commits `d92053120e` and `85a77b9cc8` preserve the transition from the retired manual-signature close gate.\n- Clarify the Git 2.38 requirement without weakening it. Ticket `pugnacious-soaplike-blackfish` rejected test skips and established the development and CI floor. The optional S3 repair implementation also uses `git merge-tree --write-tree`. The README currently calls 2.38 both a system prerequisite and a development requirement, while `docs/s3-backend.md` omits the feature requirement.\n\nRejected F02, F03, and F04 mechanisms remain excluded. No prose validator, character restriction, or mechanical writing-rule enforcement is proposed. Deferred F05 remains excluded from decision."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787405150058801001,"uuid":"0e6708ae-d1f7-4ad5-94b9-357391e48e91"}